*.synctex.gz

# ---------- 11. Superseded manuscript copies (kept on disk, deliberately not published) ----------
# Main v2 is the only manuscript published here. `papers/main/` is the 2026-09-15
# v1 draft; `papers/main_v2/sections/*.md` are frozen Markdown mirrors that hold
# pre-correction numbers; `overleaf_package.zip` is a 2026-09-16 snapshot that
# predates the 2026-10-05 numeric rebuild. Publishing any of these next to
# Main v2 would place contradictory numbers in one repository, which the
# integrity rules in docs/42_academic_integrity_and_writing_standards.md forbid.
/papers/main/
/papers/main_v2/overleaf_package.zip
/papers/main_v2/sections/*.md
# Superseded manuscript generations: v7 and bench_v2 are the published versions;
# carrying v4-v6 beside them would put contradictory numbers in one repository.
/papers/main_v4/
/papers/main_v4_zh/
/papers/main_v5/
/papers/main_v5_zh/
/papers/main_v6/
/papers/main_v6_zh/
/papers/现在评价.md
# Third-party code is cloned, not vendored: a nested .git would be added as a
# gitlink and break a fresh clone. The pinned commit lives in docs/49.
/program/third_party/
/papers/arxiv_v7.zip
/papers/arxiv_bench_v2.zip
# arXiv upload staging directories duplicate the tracked sources above.
/papers/arxiv_v7/
/papers/arxiv_bench_v2/
# Superseded benchmark manuscript generations.
/papers/bench_v1/
/papers/bench_v1_1/
# A duplicate build of the v9 PDF (main.pdf is the tracked one).
/papers/main_v9/v9.pdf

# ---------- 12. Artifact archives (published out of band) ----------
# The zip is uploaded to Zenodo; its checksums and README are versioned so the
# archive can be verified without storing 67 MiB in git history.
/release/*.zip
